# Loaded automatically by `next build`/`next start` (NODE_ENV=production) -
# see .env.example for the full explanation of this variable and how it's
# used. This file, unlike .env.local, IS meant to be committed: it's what a
# real production build (CI/deploy, not a developer's own machine) actually
# uses, since .env.local doesn't exist there. .env.local still overrides
# this on a machine where both are present - see the precedence note in
# .env.example - so a developer testing a "production" build locally against
# their own LAN IP needs to unset NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL there first.
#
# TEMPORARY: pointing at the Railway-issued URL, not api.grabmyseats.com -
# the custom domain has no DNS configured yet, so api.grabmyseats.com isn't
# live/reachable. Revert this to https://api.grabmyseats.com once the
# custom domain is actually wired up on Railway.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://grabmyseats-production.up.railway.app
